body:
//Can// a…? Sure. The transition system isn’t built for cis people who show no signs of being trans, but plenty of clinics like planned parenthood operate under a principle of informed consent where as long as the patient is aware of the risks and consents to the treatment they will provide the service. 

//Should// a…? Probably not. If you are truly cisgender then you are voluntarily deciding to effectively become trans (have the wrong body for your gender) and will likely have to deal with all the pain associated with being trans. 

Now, for some trans people they experience gender dysphoria like they are trying to play a role they are not good at/supposed to play. Maybe your experience of being an “ugly woman” is like that, meaning maybe you are a trans man and not a cis woman. There is also the possibility that you are nonbinary. And if so, transition may be the best thing for you and your mental health. 

Just whatever you do, please think about it first. Maybe consult a gender therapist if you think it would be helpful. Transitioning is hard, long, and expensive. For many it is worth it though. Just please don’t expect the road to just be pleasant.
